* SubBass HW1 - local functional models for a concrete component proposal.
* These are NOT vendor macromodels, transistor-level verification or hardware signoff.
* LTC2909 model implements only SEL=open (+UV/-UV), TMR=ZREF (internal timeout).
* External resistor dividers, shunt feed, clamps and bypass parts are on the schematic.
* Threshold/time parameters permit documented corner studies, not statistical yield.
.SUBCKT LTC2909_STUDY ADJ1 ADJ2 REF ZREF RST VCC TMR SEL PARAMS: VTH=0.5 VREF=1 UVLO=2.213 TRESET=200m TPD=500u
BSHUNT VCC ZREF I={max(0,(V(VCC,ZREF)-6.5)/10)}
BREF REF ZREF V={VREF*min(1,max(0,V(VCC,ZREF)/UVLO))}
BIQ VCC ZREF I={250u*min(1,max(0,V(VCC,ZREF)/.5))}
BSEL SEL ZREF V={min(.9,max(0,V(VCC,ZREF)))}
* Matched transmission line approximates a pessimistic 500us detection delay.
* Actual glitch rejection is amplitude-dependent; see datasheet, not a pure delay.
BVALID RAW ZREF V={(V(ADJ1,ZREF)>=VTH && V(ADJ2,ZREF)<=VTH && V(VCC,ZREF)>UVLO) ? 10 : 0}
RLOGIC RAW LIN 1k
TLOGIC LIN ZREF VALID ZREF Z0=1k TD={TPD}
RTERM VALID ZREF 1k
BCHARGE CHARGE ZREF V={V(VALID,ZREF)>2.5 ? 5 : 0}
RTIME CHARGE TIMER {TRESET/1u}
CTIME TIMER ZREF 1u
* Strong reset, without assuming a real exposed capacitor on the internal timer.
BRESET TIMER ZREF I={V(VALID,ZREF)<2.5 ? V(TIMER,ZREF) : 0}
BOD RST ZREF I={V(RST,ZREF)*((V(VALID,ZREF)>2.5 && V(TIMER,ZREF)>3.160602794 && V(VCC,ZREF)>UVLO) ? 1e-12 : .025)}
.ENDS LTC2909_STUDY

* TSSOP-16 pin order follows the actual ADG5412F package, not LFCSP numbering.
* Constant RON, bounded off leakage, approximate capacitance and supply interlock.
* Missing: charge injection, detailed Ron curvature, noise, THD, real propagation.
* Charge injection is assessed separately as an imposed charge packet in verification.
.SUBCKT ADG5412F_STUDY IN1 D1 S1 VSS ZREF S4 D4 IN4 IN3 D3 S3 FF VDD S2 D2 IN2 PARAMS: RON=10 IOFF=5n CFEED=1p
BPATH1 S1 D1 I={V(S1,D1)*((V(IN1,ZREF)>2 && V(VDD,VSS)>=8 && V(S1,ZREF)>=V(VSS,ZREF)-.7 && V(S1,ZREF)<=V(VDD,ZREF)+.7) ? 1/RON : 1e-9)}
BPATH2 S2 D2 I={V(S2,D2)*((V(IN2,ZREF)>2 && V(VDD,VSS)>=8) ? 1/RON : 1e-9)}
BPATH3 S3 D3 I={V(S3,D3)*((V(IN3,ZREF)>2 && V(VDD,VSS)>=8) ? 1/RON : 1e-9)}
BPATH4 S4 D4 I={V(S4,D4)*((V(IN4,ZREF)>2 && V(VDD,VSS)>=8) ? 1/RON : 1e-9)}
BLEAK ZREF D1 I={V(IN1,ZREF)<.8 || V(VDD,VSS)<8 ? IOFF : 0}
DDHI D1 VDD DRAIN_ESD
DDLO VSS D1 DRAIN_ESD
.MODEL DRAIN_ESD D(IS=1e-14 N=1.2 RS=1)
CSD S1 D1 {CFEED}
CD D1 ZREF 24p
BIN IN1 ZREF I={V(IN1,ZREF)>0.1 ? 1.2u : 0}
BFF FF ZREF V={V(VDD,VSS)>=8 ? 3 : 0}
BIP VDD ZREF I={.4m*min(1,max(0,V(VDD,VSS)/8))}
BIB VDD VSS I={.5m*min(1,max(0,V(VDD,VSS)/8))}
.ENDS ADG5412F_STUDY

* Approximate BAT54WS Schottky model. Verify cold clamp voltage in the prototype.
.SUBCKT BAT54WS_STUDY K A
DCLAMP A K BAT54_APPROX
.MODEL BAT54_APPROX D(IS=200n N=1.06 RS=2 CJO=10p BV=30 IBV=2u)
.ENDS BAT54WS_STUDY

* TLV1702 fast fault path. Static smooth threshold approximation to keep
* convergence robust; actual 560 ns is typical at 100 mV, no guaranteed max.
.SUBCKT TLV1702_FAST_STUDY OUT1 IN1M IN1P VSS IN2P IN2M OUT2 VCC
BFAIL1 FAIL1 VSS V={1/(1+exp(min(40,max(-40,(V(IN1P,VSS)-V(IN1M,VSS))*1000))))}
BFAIL2 FAIL2 VSS V={1/(1+exp(min(40,max(-40,(V(IN2P,VSS)-V(IN2M,VSS))*1000))))}
BOUT1 OUT1 VSS I={V(OUT1,VSS)*(V(VCC,VSS)>2.2 ? V(FAIL1,VSS)/25 : 1e-12)}
BOUT2 OUT2 VSS I={V(OUT2,VSS)*(V(VCC,VSS)>2.2 ? V(FAIL2,VSS)/25 : 1e-12)}
.ENDS TLV1702_FAST_STUDY
